      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Major Charles Dunwody, whose name was misspelled on a banking note, adding an extra “o.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunwoody%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ebenezer Primitive Baptist Church, built in 1829, stands as Dunwoody’s oldest building and a living piece of early history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoverdunwoody.com/about-dunwoody/history-of-dunwoody/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Roswell Railroad, opened in 1881, ran through Dunwoody, turning the area into a small crossroads community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunwoody%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dunwoody hosts the only MARTA subway station within its limits, while nearby stations lie just outside the city border.",
